ed ratification. The unresolved security defect is the false browser affordance for a departed requester, which invites a signature and records a durable ineffective act. Role satisfiers fail closed because departed actors hold no roles; originating-requester is the uncovered path. Citation text is React-escaped, causal references are bounded, and no secret-handling change was found.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Projecting one captured field and consuming it through one authority helper is the simplest honest design; replaying vocabulary in the browser would be worse. The citation composer correctly uses one bases value for disclosure and submission. No fluff needs removal. The two repairs are small: make the requester membership check fold-equivalent, and make the existing cache witness test the transition its own comment requires.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD. npm test --prefix ui passed 96 of 96. gofmt -l was empty. go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 ./..., make ui-check, git diff --check, and the post-build internal/service/uidist byte comparison all passed. The worktree was clean before and after; HEAD equals origin/request/decision-records-ui-authorized. Targeted admission-time, rendered citation, and cache tests also pass, but the cache test passes on the wrong predecessor shape.\n\nFRESH THIS PASS: both blockers, the departed-requester reproduction, admission/citation code inspection, golden inspection, scope rulings, and all gates above. CARRIED FORWARD, NOT RE-DERIVED: the receipt-checkpoint behavior in base 10c6d623, which already has its own approved and ratified exact-head review.\n\nDo not merge this head. Publish a repaired exact head with fresh artifacts and request a fresh independent review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5d42f1604e6906a08a048b1c74803e44babb0e8f","head":"477637589ee395b996dd1c16ca7c93ee132de486","verdict":"changes-requested"}}